       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, those effects can last for days. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO daily.** This is the usual starting dose. Use 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily.** This is the maximum recommended dose.\n- **50 mg is intended.** Tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order."
